<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5583" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμύκλαι</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶν</span>,
			αἱ, <u>Amyclae</u> in Laconia,
		famous for worship of Apollo, <i><span class="en">
			Il.
		</span></i>, etc.:—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμυκλ-αῖος</span></b> , or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμυ-αεύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Amyclean,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.5.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				532
			</span></i>:— <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αῖον, τό,</span>
			<i>temple of Amyclean Apollo,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν Ἀ.</span> Foed. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.18
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				23
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῷ Ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					6.3.2
				</span></i>
			; of Artemis, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Aet.</u>
				1.1.24
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμύ-ᾱθεν</span></b> 
			<i>from Amyclae,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				11.34
			</span></i>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμύκλαι</span></b> , αἱ, sort of <i>shoes,</i> named after
				<i>Amyclae,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				10.35
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμυ-ᾷδες</span></b> , αἱ, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				44D.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.Com.
				5
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.88
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμυκλαϊάζω</span></b> , <i>speak in
				the Amyclean</i> (i.e. <i>Laconian) dialect,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				12.13
			</span></i>.</div>
